---
id: RL-003
type: rule
family: responsibility-laundering
title: Blanket unrelated dismissal
version: 1

severity: error
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 1

targets: [agent-output, pr-description]

detection:
  type: regex
  pattern: (?i)\b(all|every)\s+(ci\s+)?(failures?|checks?)\s+(are|is)\s+(pre-existing|unrelated|not\s+related)

related: [RL-001, RL-004]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

Dismissing all failures at once means no per-failure analysis was done.
Each failure must be verified individually against the base branch.

Don't say "all CI failures are pre-existing." Instead, list each failure,
check whether it reproduces on main, and report findings per failure.
Blanket claims hide real issues behind confident language.
